1. Scope and definitions

"Software" means the original supr-meow-vela source code, mining and inference
kernels, binaries, and accompanying materials supplied under this license.
Separately licensed third-party components and models are excluded.

A "Derivative Miner" is other mining or verification software that copies, adapts,
incorporates, or links to any substantial portion of the Software, including
its source, compiled kernels, or other compiled code. Running or compiling the
unmodified Software as permitted in section 2(a) does not create a Derivative
Miner and is not subject to the commercial-incorporation restriction.

A "Commercial Miner" is a Derivative Miner sold, licensed for payment, offered
as a paid software product or service, or monetized through a developer fee,
mandatory donation, subscription, royalty, or paid feature. Merely earning
mining rewards by operating the Software as permitted in section 2 is not
commercial exploitation of the Software for this definition.

A "Closed-Source Miner" is a Derivative Miner for which the complete preferred
source for modification, including changes and the scripts needed to build
it, is not publicly available without charge under this license. Independent
third-party dependencies may retain their own licenses and source locations.

2. Permissions

Subject to the conditions below, you may:

(a) download, inspect, compile, and run the unmodified Software for mining or
    verification, including for profit and on hardware you own or manage;
(b) modify the Software for private evaluation, research, and testing;
(c) redistribute unmodified copies without a software license charge, retaining
    this license, copyright notices, and third-party notices, and providing the
    corresponding source or a working public link to that exact source; and
(d) develop, use, and distribute a non-commercial Derivative Miner whose complete
    corresponding source is publicly available under this same license. Mark
    modifications clearly and retain the original copyright and notices.

3. Commercial and closed-source incorporation prohibited

Without prior written permission from ocminer / suprnova, you must not copy,
adapt, incorporate, link, redistribute, or otherwise use the Software or any
substantial portion of it to develop or operate a Commercial Miner or a
Closed-Source Miner. Making source visible does not permit a Commercial Miner.
Distributing a binary without charge does not permit a Closed-Source Miner.
The private evaluation permission in section 2(b) does not permit deployment
or distribution of a Commercial Miner or Closed-Source Miner.

This restriction covers incorporation into another miner through source code,
libraries, compiled kernels, or other compiled components. It does not claim
ownership of independently implemented protocols, mathematical ideas, or
separately licensed third-party material.

